  culture: `<p>Bargaining is normal in markets, with taxi drivers and at small shops without price tags, but not in supermarkets, pharmacies or chain stores. Keep it friendly and joking. <i>3ashaanak</i> (“for your sake”) is how the seller signals the final price. Coins are rare; carry small notes (5, 10, 20).</p>`,
